// LEVEL: 1
// DEPENDENCE: ./src
// Regression: cjlint must not be silent on source files that contain compile
// errors. The same file fed to cjc reports: (1) "the visibility of an 'open'
// function must be 'public' or 'protected'" and (2) "undeclared identifier
// 'undeclaredFunc'", while cjlint exits 0 without any diagnostic and the
// valid G.VAR.01 warning is swallowed as well (a broken package must not
// look clean).
// NOTE: the 'undeclared identifier' assertion is mandatory under any design:
// skipping semantic-analysis-dependent rules on broken code may be an
// acceptable trade-off, but it must be visible (errors reported / exit code).
// The G.VAR.01 assertion is the strict expectation; it may be relaxed only
// together with explicit compile-error reporting being added.
// EXEC-PIPE: %lint -f ./src -c %cangjieDir/tools -m %cangjieDir 2>&1 | compare %f
// ASSERT: regex .*undeclared identifier.*
// ASSERT: regex .*G\.VAR\.01.*
